.TH CMAAL 1 "" "cmaal @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cmaal \- a multitool for Arch Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cmaal
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ arguments ...]
.br
.B cmaal
.RB { \-S | \-Ss | \-Si | \-Syu | \-Syyu | \-R ...}
.RI [ package ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cmaal
is one command for everything package related on Arch Linux. It looks for
packages in the official repositories (pacman), then the AUR (through yay,
paru or pikaur), then flatpak, and installs each one from wherever it is
found. It also manages SSH hosts, rolls back upgrades, cleans the system and
keeps itself up to date.
.PP
Any pacman style flag cmaal does not handle itself is passed straight to
the AUR helper, or to pacman when there is none.
.PP
Add
.B \-\-noconfirm
to any command to skip questions. cmaal then takes each question's default
answer, like pacman does.
.SH PACKAGE COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "\-S " package...
Install packages from the official repos, the AUR or flatpak, whichever has
them. Without a package name, opens an fzf picker over every available
package (Tab selects several, a preview shows details).
.TP
.BI "\-Ss " query
Search the repos, the AUR and flatpak at once.
.TP
.BI "\-Si " package
Package information from any source.
.TP
.BR \-Syu ", " \-Syyu ", " upgrade
Upgrade repos, AUR and flatpak. Before upgrading, unread Arch news is shown
and a snapper or timeshift snapshot is taken (see
.BR SNAPSHOT_BEFORE_UPGRADE ).
Afterwards cmaal lists
.I .pacnew
files and tells you when a reboot is needed.
.TP
.RB "\-Rns " [ \fIpackage\fR ...]
Remove packages. Without a name, opens an fzf picker over explicitly
installed packages and flatpaks.
.TP
.B updates
List pending updates without installing anything. Uses
.BR checkupdates (8)
when pacman-contrib is installed.
.TP
.BI "why " package
Why a package is installed: by you or as a dependency, and what needs it.
.TP
.BI "files " package
Files a package installs, whether it is installed or not.
.TP
.BI "provides " command|file
Which package provides a command you don't have yet (uses the pacman file
database, downloaded on first use).
.TP
.BI "owns " command|file
Which installed package a command or file belongs to.
.TP
.BI "pkgbuild " package
Show the build script of a repo or AUR package. Read AUR PKGBUILDs before
installing them.
.TP
.RB "orphans " [ rm ]
List dependencies nothing needs anymore, and remove them with
.BR rm .
.TP
.RI "big " [ n ]
The largest installed packages.
.TP
.RB "helper " [ "install yay" | "install paru" ]
Show the AUR helper in use, or build and install one.
.SH ROLLBACK COMMANDS
.TP
.B undo
Revert the last pacman transaction: restore upgraded and removed packages
from the package cache (or the Arch Linux Archive) and remove newly
installed ones. Running it again redoes the change.
.TP
.BI "downgrade " package
Pick an older version from the package cache or the Arch Linux Archive.
.TP
.BI "hold " package...
Keep packages at their current version by adding them to
.B IgnorePkg
in
.IR /etc/pacman.conf .
The edited file is validated with
.BR pacman-conf (8)
and a backup is kept at
.IR /etc/pacman.conf.cmaal.bak .
.TP
.BI "unhold " package...
Let held packages upgrade again.
.TP
.B holds
List held packages.
.TP
.RB "snapshot " [ list | create " [\fIdescription\fR] | " restore ]
Manage snapper or timeshift snapshots.
.TP
.RB "pkglist " export | import " [\fIfile\fR]"
Save every package you installed (repo, AUR, flatpak) to a file, or install
everything from such a file. The default file is
.IR ~/cmaal-packages.txt .
.TP
.RI "history " [ n ]
Recent installs, upgrades and removals from the pacman log.
.SH SYSTEM COMMANDS
.TP
.B clean
Remove orphans, trim the package cache, AUR build caches, unused flatpak
runtimes and the systemd journal. Asks before each step.
.TP
.B fix
Fix common pacman problems: a leftover database lock, keyring and signature
errors, a dead mirror, database inconsistencies and packages with missing
files.
.TP
.RI "mirrors " [ country ]
Rank the fastest mirrors with
.BR reflector (1).
The old mirrorlist is kept as
.IR mirrorlist.bak .
.TP
.RI "news " [ n ]
Latest Arch Linux news.
.TP
.RB "services " [ \-\-user "] [\fIname\fR] [\fIaction\fR]"
Pick a systemd service, then status, start, stop, restart, enable, disable
or logs.
.TP
.RI "logs " [ unit | prev | \-f ]
Errors from the journal since boot, from the previous boot, for one unit, or
followed live.
.TP
.B kernel
Running and installed kernels, and whether a reboot is needed.
.TP
.B disk
Disk usage, caches you can clean and the biggest folders in your home.
.TP
.B ports
Which programs listen on which ports.
.TP
.B ip
Local and public IP addresses.
.TP
.BR sys ", " fetch
System overview; fetch shows it next to the Arch logo.
.TP
.B doctor
Check optional tools and system health.
.SH SSH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ssh
Pick a saved host (fzf if installed) and connect. Inside kitty, cmaal
connects with
.B kitten ssh
so the server learns kitty's terminal type.
.TP
.RB "ssh " [ \-t ] " \fIhost\fR [\fIargs\fR]"
Connect to a host.
.B \-t
opens it in a new kitty tab (needs
.B allow_remote_control yes
in kitty.conf).
.TP
.B ssh ls \fR|\fB add \fR|\fB rm \fR|\fB edit
List, add, remove or edit hosts in
.IR ~/.ssh/config .
.TP
.B ssh keygen \fR|\fB keys \fR|\fB copy \fR|\fB test
Create an ed25519 key, list keys, copy a key to a server, test key login.
.TP
.B ssh server on \fR|\fB off \fR|\fB status
Manage the local sshd.
.SH OTHER COMMANDS
.TP
.RI "theme " [ name ]
Pick or switch the kitty color theme.
.TP
.RI "weather " [ city ]
Weather forecast from wttr.in.
.TP
.RB "self\-update " [ \-\-force ]
Update cmaal. For a package install this rebuilds the package with
.BR makepkg (8).
.TP
.RI "whatsnew " [ version | all ]
What changed in a version.
.TP
.RB "config " [ edit | show | path | reset ]
Edit or inspect the configuration file.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove cmaal (with pacman for a package install).
.TP
.RI "help " [ word ]
Show help, or only the lines matching a word.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are read from
.IR ~/.config/cmaal/config ,
a bash file.
.B cmaal config
creates it from the defaults in
.IR /usr/share/cmaal/config.default .
.TP
.B AUTO_UPDATE
.BR notify " (default), " auto " or " off .
.TP
.B UPDATE_INTERVAL_HOURS
How often to check for a new cmaal version (default 24).
.TP
.B AUR_HELPER
.BR auto ", " yay ", " paru ", " pikaur " or " none .
.TP
.B USE_FLATPAK
Include flatpak in search, install and upgrades
.RB ( yes / no ).
.TP
.B SHOW_NEWS_ON_UPGRADE
Show unread Arch news before upgrading
.RB ( yes / no ).
.TP
.B SNAPSHOT_BEFORE_UPGRADE
.BR auto ", " yes " or " no .
.B auto
skips it when snap-pac or timeshift-autosnap already snapshot.
.TP
.B SSH_USE_KITTEN
Use kitten ssh:
.BR auto ", " yes " or " no .
.TP
.B SSH_NEW_TAB
Always open ssh hosts in a new kitty tab
.RB ( yes / no ).
.TP
.B WEATHER_CITY
Default city for
.BR "cmaal weather" .
.TP
.B NOTIFY_AFTER_SECONDS
Desktop notification when an upgrade takes longer than this (0 = never).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/cmaal
The command.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/cmaal/
The modules that implement the commands.
.TP
.I ~/.config/cmaal/config
Your settings.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/cmaal/
Update check, seen news and the AUR package list.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colored output.
.TP
.B CMAAL_BRANCH
Branch used by self-update (default main).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B cmaal \-S discord visual\-studio\-code\-bin spotify
Installs from pacman, the AUR and flatpak in one go.
.TP
.B cmaal downgrade mesa && cmaal hold mesa
Go back to an older mesa and keep it there.
.TP
.B cmaal provides htop
Find out which package gives you the htop command.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8),
.BR makepkg (8),
.BR yay (8),
.BR paru (8),
.BR flatpak (1),
.BR reflector (1),
.BR kitty (1)
.PP
https://github.com/archlinux\-dev/cmaal
